@OS_NAME@ @VERSION@ for the @MODEL_NAME@: SD card image
================================================================

pocket-ui is a game launcher with its own libretro frontend. This card (pocket-ui @VERSION@) starts it when the
handheld boots from it. The handheld's own system stays as it is: it lives on the card the handheld came with, and
nothing is flashed to the handheld (the R36S has no internal memory).

This card is a beta: the @MODEL_NAME@ is new to pocket-ui, and so far it has been started on few of them. Please report
what works and what doesn't (@ISSUES_URL@). It is for the genuine R36S (ROCKNIX's "a" image); clones that ROCKNIX starts with its "b" image are not covered.
#if DEVTEST

DEVICE TEST CARD: this card also turns on ROCKNIX's USB network (USB_MODE=cdc) and SSH, and lets in the SSH key of the
computer it was built on. Connect the R36S's USB-C port to that computer: the handheld is 169.254.170.2 and gives the
computer 169.254.170.1, then `ssh root@169.254.170.2` works with that key (and ROCKNIX's root password "rocknix").
While the port is a network, a USB Wi-Fi adapter on it does not work. Only for our own device tests: never hand this card
out; use the normal card (without -devtest) for anyone else.
#endif

@OS_NAME@ is built on ROCKNIX @ROCKNIX_TAG@ (https://rocknix.org): its kernel, system and emulators are
ROCKNIX's. pocket-ui is not made or endorsed by the ROCKNIX team; please report problems with this card to
pocket-ui (@ISSUES_URL@), not to ROCKNIX.


Install
-------

1. Write @IMAGE_NAME@.img.xz to a microSD card with balenaEtcher or Raspberry Pi
   Imager. Both read the .xz file directly. Everything on the card is erased. 8 GB or more.
   Use a spare card, not the one the handheld came with: that card is the handheld's own system.
2. Take the original card out, put this one into the first card slot (TF1) of the switched-off handheld and switch it on.
3. The first start shows some text on a dark screen and restarts once by itself while the card is set up: don't switch
   off. If it does lose power, just switch it on again: it carries on from where it stopped.
   Then pocket-ui's first-start setup opens. The pause menu (HOME) is the FN key.
4. To go back to the handheld's own system, switch off, take this card out and put the original card back. Keep it safe.


Black screen?
-------------

R36S made from 2024 on often have a newer screen that needs one extra file. The handheld is fine; only the picture is missing.
No computer needed if you still have the original card: put it into the second slot (TF2) and switch on again. The card reads
the screen from the original card (only reads it, changes nothing there), starts again once, and the picture is there.
Otherwise switch off (hold Power for 10 seconds) and put the card into a computer. On its ROCKNIX drive:
  - Easiest, if you still have the original card: copy the .dtb file from the original card's first drive into the
    folder stock/ on this card and start the R36S. The card reads the screen from it, writes overlays/mipi-panel.dtbo,
    starts again once and notes what it did in stock/panel-log.txt.
  - Or copy one file from r36s-panels/ into overlays/ and rename it to mipi-panel.dtbo (r36s-panels/README.txt says which
    to try first). Still black? Try the next one.
To go back to the original screen, delete overlays/mipi-panel.dtbo.


Add your games
--------------

The R36S has no Wi-Fi chip, so the Wi-Fi ways in (file sharing, updates over the air) need a USB Wi-Fi adapter on its
USB-C port. Without one: put your games on a second microSD card in the second slot (TF2; ROCKNIX uses it for games and
makes a "roms" folder on it), or switch off and copy them onto this card's STORAGE from a Linux computer.
Settings, Games, Add games shows the folder of each system.

Your computer can't write to the card's large STORAGE part without extra software, and Windows may ask to format it:
never say yes, press Cancel. Formatting would erase pocket-ui from the card.

This card starts the R36S's own device tree: ROCKNIX's boot script has no R36S entry, so extlinux/extlinux.conf names
@DTB_NAME@.dtb (what ROCKNIX's own extlinux/extlinux.conf.r36s says). Nothing to change. If it stays black with every screen
file, switch off (hold Power for 10 seconds) and report it.

This card contains no games and no console maker's BIOS files (the one BIOS in it is DraStic's open replacement). Add only games and BIOS files you own.
#if DEVTEST
On this device test card SSH is on from the start (see above); file sharing and Syncthing are off.
#else
Remote access (SSH), file sharing and Syncthing are off. When you turn on Remote access or file
sharing in pocket-ui's Settings, it makes a password for this device and shows it on the screen.
(EmulationStation, ROCKNIX's menu, can also turn SSH on; it then uses ROCKNIX's standard root password
"rocknix" until you change it there.)
#endif
Updates come from pocket-ui (Settings, Updates). Without Wi-Fi, update from a card: download the update file
pocket-ui-update-<version>-rocknix.zip from pocketui.xyz/install, copy it (don't unzip it) onto the second card in TF2 or
onto this card's ROCKNIX drive, and switch on: pocket-ui offers the update, press A. Your games, saves and settings stay.
Settings, System, Updates, Look on the card does the same at any time. ROCKNIX's own updates would replace the system and the
U-Boot on this card behind pocket-ui's back, so this card does not install them: the boot hook moves
any update pocket-ui did not check (from EmulationStation's menu, the network share "update" or copied
by hand) to /storage/.update-refused and starts as usual. Nothing there is deleted.


What is on the card
-------------------

Before the first partition (the card's first 16 MiB): ROCKNIX's legacy U-Boot from its "a" image
(ROCKNIX-RK3326.aarch64-@ROCKNIX_TAG@-a.img.gz), unchanged.

FAT partition "ROCKNIX" (readable on any computer):
  KERNEL, KERNEL.md5         ROCKNIX @ROCKNIX_TAG@, unchanged
  SYSTEM, SYSTEM.md5         ROCKNIX @ROCKNIX_TAG@'s system, repacked without the files listed under
                             "Changes" below; everything else in it is unchanged
  *.dtb, boot.scr, overlays/, stock/   ROCKNIX's, unchanged (overlays/ holds no screen file)
  extlinux/extlinux.conf     ROCKNIX's, with one line changed: FDT /@DTB_NAME@.dtb (ROCKNIX's image has
                             that line commented out; its boot script would pick the R33S's tree)
  r36s-panels/               screen files for the newer R36S screens, and a README (see "Black screen?")
  post-flash.sh              boot hook: starts without the ROCKNIX logo
  mount-storage.sh           boot hook: puts pocket-ui's start entry in place once the storage has
                             grown; at every start, sets aside system updates pocket-ui did not check
  pocket-ui-info/            this file; SOURCE-OFFER.txt; pocket-ui-os.txt (name and version, shown
                             in Settings, About); pocket-ui's LICENSE and NOTICE.md;
                             licences/ (the Rust crates' licence texts and the fonts' OFL; /storage/pocket-ui/licences
                             links here); rocknix-licenses/ (ROCKNIX's
                             LICENSE.md and licenses folder at tag @ROCKNIX_TAG@); firmware-licences/
                             (the terms of the firmware files inside SYSTEM)

Partition "STORAGE" (grows to fill the card at the first start):
  pocket-ui/                 pocket-ui, pocket-core and pocket-splash (the boot screen) @VERSION@, the launcher
  .pocket-seed/              the start entry for pocket-ui and the boot screen's unit (moved to
                             .config/system.d at the second start), a script ROCKNIX runs once
                             at the first start (device name "@HOSTNAME@", ROCKNIX's update check off), and the
                             screen script that reads a tree in stock/ (ROCKNIX's importpanel.py, screen only)
#if DEVTEST
                             and, on this device test card only: ROCKNIX's USB network setting, the build computer's
                             public SSH key (.ssh/authorized_keys), pocket-ui's dev-ssh marker and a script that keeps
                             SSH and the USB network on
#endif

Changes from the ROCKNIX image: the files above were added (the hooks, r36s-panels/, pocket-ui-info/, pocket-ui/) and the
one line in extlinux.conf changed.
Removed from SYSTEM:
  - the Kickstart relocation tables (kick*.RTB) of Amiberry's WHDLoad booter, loose and inside its
    boot-data.zip (the rest of that archive is unchanged). They come from SKick
    (aminet.net, util/boot/skick346.lha), whose licence allows passing them on only inside that unchanged
    archive. Amiga games run with the standard emulator as before; for WHDLoad games in Amiberry,
    copy the .RTB files from that archive to /storage/.config/amiberry/whdboot/save-data/Kickstarts.
  - the DOOM shareware game data (usr/share/idtech/doom.tar.gz), so the card holds no games; its
    shareware terms also ask for the complete, unchanged shareware package.
The partition table (but for the STORAGE partition's size), KERNEL and the U-Boot are unchanged. ROCKNIX's own interface,
EmulationStation, stays on the card and takes over if pocket-ui cannot start.


Licences
--------

This image may be shared free of charge, for non-commercial use only. Do not sell it, and do not
bundle it with hardware you sell. Reasons: ROCKNIX includes components licensed for non-commercial use
only (for example the libretro cores snes9x, genesis_plus_gx, picodrive and fbneo), and its artwork is
licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.

ROCKNIX (KERNEL, SYSTEM)
  Copyright ROCKNIX (https://github.com/ROCKNIX). ROCKNIX is a fork of JELOS
  (https://github.com/JustEnoughLinuxOS/distribution); credit to the JELOS team.
  The ROCKNIX team's own software and scripts: GNU GPL version 2. Every bundled component keeps its own
  licence: see pocket-ui-info/rocknix-licenses/ (ROCKNIX's LICENSE.md and licenses folder) and each
  package's PKG_LICENSE in ROCKNIX's source.
  ROCKNIX branding and images (logos, splash artwork, EmulationStation themes inside SYSTEM):
  CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/ . They are included unchanged
  inside SYSTEM; this image does not use them as its own branding.

Firmware inside SYSTEM (usr/lib/kernel-overlays/base/lib/firmware): 295 files, unchanged; nearly all are byte for byte
  linux-firmware 20260309's and the wireless regulatory database. pocket-ui-info/firmware-licences/README.txt lists
  every file with its terms. Still open: 10 files are not traced to a source with stated terms
  (Realtek Bluetooth files and the ESP8089 Wi-Fi files for some clones), and the terms of the Mali GPU driver in SYSTEM
  (libmali) have not been read yet.

Screen overlays (r36s-panels/ on the FAT partition): ROCKNIX's prebuilt files for the newer R36S screens, unchanged, from
  https://github.com/stolen/rnix/releases/tag/panel_overlays (a fork of ROCKNIX's repository; no licence of their own is
  stated for these files). They hold a screen's start-up commands and timings.

Linux kernel (KERNEL): GNU GPL version 2. The device trees (*.dtb in the FAT root) are ROCKNIX's, unchanged.

U-Boot (on the card before the first partition, and usr/share/bootloader in SYSTEM): ROCKNIX's legacy U-Boot
  (Hardkernel's, ROCKNIX/hardkernel-uboot), GNU GPL version 2 or later, with Rockchip's loader parts (rkbin); built by
  ROCKNIX, source and recipes in ROCKNIX's repository at the tag below. boot.scr is ROCKNIX's, unchanged.

DraStic (usr/config/drastic in SYSTEM): the Nintendo DS emulator DraStic by Exophase (https://www.drastic-ds.com/) is
  closed-source software. It is passed on unchanged, as ROCKNIX does, on the basis of the author's 2017 forum
  statement that there is "no real harm" in distributing it (usr/config/drastic/LICENSE.pdf, and ROCKNIX's
  pocket-ui-info/rocknix-licenses/licenses/DRASTIC.pdf). That is a tolerance, not a formal licence, and no source
  code for it exists. Credit: Exophase. We remove it from the image on request of the author.
  Its BIOS replacement (drastic_bios_arm7.bin, drastic_bios_arm9.bin) is open: Gilead Kutnick, BSD licence, text in
  usr/config/drastic/system/drastic_bios_readme.txt.

pocket-ui and pocket-core
  GNU GPL version 2 or later (pocket-ui-info/LICENSE).
  Source: @POCKET_UI_SOURCE@.
  Third-party credits (fonts, Rust crates and other parts, each under its own licence) are in
  NOTICE.md: pocket-ui-info/NOTICE.md on this card, and in the repository. The licence texts of the Rust crates
  and of the fonts (SIL Open Font License) are in pocket-ui-info/licences/.


Source code
-----------

pocket-ui's source and the scripts that build this image are next to the image on @RELEASE_URL@
(pocket-ui-@VERSION@-src.tar.gz); the rest of the source is public at the links below. For at least three
years from the release of this image, anyone can ask for the complete corresponding source code of the GNU GPL
and LGPL software on this card, for no charge beyond the cost of providing it: open an issue at the project's
GitHub page. See pocket-ui-info/SOURCE-OFFER.txt.

ROCKNIX @ROCKNIX_TAG@, including the kernel and its patches:
  https://github.com/ROCKNIX/distribution/tree/@ROCKNIX_TAG@
  tag @ROCKNIX_TAG@, commit @ROCKNIX_COMMIT@
pocket-ui, pocket-core and the scripts that make this image: @POCKET_UI_SOURCE@
  (scripts/make-image-family.sh --family RK3326 rebuilds this image from the ROCKNIX release above;
  scripts/check-image-family.sh checks it).
